WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.312
Priya: Okay, we're keeping the read-only scope. Today's standup has a ten-minute hard stop.

2
00:00:06.312 --> 00:00:13.272
Lukas: Does that exclude editing inventory records? Review complexity changes if writes sneak in.

3
00:00:13.272 --> 00:00:20.927
Raj: Yes, listing and filtering records only. Just to confirm, bulk updates stay out, right?

4
00:00:20.927 --> 00:00:27.167
Anika: The demo should show two inventory pages. Maybe a third if the fixture is ready.

5
00:00:27.167 --> 00:00:34.751
Hannah: Two pages already exercise cursor handling. A third page isn't the acceptance gate.

6
00:00:34.751 --> 00:00:41.255
Priya: Good, one action item is confirming ownership. Who has bandwidth for the parser review?

7
00:00:41.255 --> 00:00:47.999
Lukas: I can review after my platform check. Send the focused change, not unrelated cleanup.

8
00:00:47.999 --> 00:00:54.742
Raj: The export feature can wait another sprint. Let's park that until this demo works.

9
00:00:54.742 --> 00:01:03.358
Hannah: I'll report test progress after the implementation. We should surface blockers before assigning more work.

10
00:01:03.358 --> 00:01:10.510
Anika: Agreed, I'll cover the API dependency next. No production rollout is planned this week.

